---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" class="min-h-screen flex flex-col">
  <main class="flex-1 container px-4 py-32">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">At a glance</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          This website is a purely informational, statically generated site. It
          does not use cookies, does not include analytics or tracking of any
          kind, does not embed third-party content, and does not offer forms
          through which you could enter personal data. All fonts, scripts, and
          images are served from this website's own domain. The only personal
          data processed in connection with this website is the technical data
          your browser transmits automatically when you visit, which is recorded
          in server log files, and any data you send us yourself if you contact
          us by email or phone. Our presences on external platforms such as
          GitHub, LinkedIn, and Matrix are covered in a separate section below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Controller</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The controller within the meaning of the EU General Data Protection
          Regulation (GDPR) is:
        </p>
        <address class="not-italic text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          Prof. Dr.-Ing. María Dolores Pérez Guirao<br />
          c/o Ostfalia Hochschule für angewandte Wissenschaften<br />
          – Hochschule Braunschweig/Wolfenbüttel<br />
          Salzdahlumer Str. 46/48<br />
          38302 Wolfenbüttel<br />
          Germany
        </address>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Phone: +49 5331 939 42690<br />
          Email:{" "}
          <a
            href="mailto:m.perez@ostfalia.de"
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          >
            m.perez@ostfalia.de
          </a>
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Impressum:{" "}
          <a href="/impressum/" class="underline hover:text-foreground">
            opener-initiative.org/impressum/
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          Hosting and server log files
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
          This website is hosted by Hetzner Online GmbH, Industriestr. 25, 91710
          Gunzenhausen, Germany. All data is processed in Hetzner's data centers
          in the European Union. Further information on data protection at
          Hetzner is available in{" "}
          <a
            href="https://www.hetzner.com/legal/privacy-policy/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          >
            Hetzner's privacy policy
          </a>.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
          When you access this website, the web server automatically records
          technical information that your browser transmits with every request.
          This includes:
        </p>
        <ul
          class="list-disc pl-6 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-1"
        >
          <li>the IP address of the requesting device,</li>
          <li>date and time of the request,</li>
          <li>the requested URL and the amount of data transferred,</li>
          <li>the HTTP status code of the response,</li>
          <li>the referrer URL (the page from which you followed a link),</li>
          <li>browser type and version, and the operating system used.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
          This data is processed to deliver the website to your device, to
          ensure the stability and security of the service, and to detect and
          investigate misuse or attacks. It is not merged with other data
          sources and is not used to identify individual visitors. The legal
          basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR: our legitimate interest in providing this
          website securely and reliably.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Server log files are deleted after 14 days at the latest, unless a
          specific incident (such as an attack on the website) requires longer
          retention as evidence.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          Hetzner processes this data on our behalf on the basis of a data
          processing agreement pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Security and encryption</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          We take appropriate technical and organizational measures in
          accordance with Art. 32 GDPR to protect the data processed when you
          visit this website. In particular, this website is delivered
          exclusively over an encrypted connection using TLS/SSL technology
          (recognizable by "https://" and the lock symbol in your browser's
          address bar), which protects the data transmitted between your browser
          and our server against unauthorized access by third parties.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          No cookies, no tracking, no analytics
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          This website does not set cookies, does not store or read any
          information on your device (§ 25 TDDDG), and does not use analytics,
          advertising, or tracking services. Fonts and all other resources are
          hosted on our own server; no connections to third-party servers are
          established when you view this site. For this reason, no consent
          banner is required or shown.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Contact by email or phone</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          If you contact us by email or phone, the data you provide (such as
          your name, email address, and the content of your message) is
          processed solely to handle your inquiry. The legal basis is Art.
          6(1)(f) GDPR (our legitimate interest in responding to inquiries) or,
          where your inquiry relates to entering into or performing a contract,
          Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR. We delete this data once your inquiry has been
          dealt with, unless statutory retention obligations require us to keep
          it longer. Please note that emails are generally encrypted in transit
          but not end-to-end; complete confidentiality of a message on its way
          to our mailbox can therefore not be guaranteed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">RSS feed</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          This website offers an RSS feed. When your feed reader retrieves the
          feed, the same technical data described under "Hosting and server log
          files" above is processed; no further data is collected.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          Presences on external platforms
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
          We maintain presences on external platforms to provide information
          about the Opener Initiative and to communicate with the community: a
          GitHub organization, a LinkedIn company page, and a Matrix room. When
          you visit or interact with these presences, the respective platform
          operator processes your data under its own privacy policy; this may
          include processing outside the European Union and, on commercial
          platforms, processing of usage data for market research and
          advertising purposes. We only receive the information that the
          platform makes available to us (such as public profiles,
          contributions, and messages addressed to us) and process it to run
          these community channels. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR: our
          legitimate interest in communicating with the community and the
          public.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
          For our LinkedIn company page, we are joint controllers with LinkedIn
          Ireland Unlimited Company (Wilton Plaza, Dublin 2, Ireland) for the
          collection of visitor data used to compile the "Page Insights"
          statistics, on the basis of the{" "}
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/legal/l/page-joint-controller-addendum"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          >
            Page Insights Joint Controller Addendum
          </a>. Any further processing is the sole responsibility of LinkedIn;
          transfers to the USA are based on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework and
          standard contractual clauses. Details can be found in{" "}
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          >
            LinkedIn's privacy policy
          </a>; LinkedIn also provides an{" "}
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/mypreferences/g/guest-retargeting-opt-out"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          >
            opt-out from its advertising tracking
          </a>.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          Since only the platform operators have full access to the data
          processed on their platforms, data-subject requests are most
          effectively addressed directly to them; you can, however, always
          contact us as well.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Links to external websites</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          This website contains links to external websites operated by third
          parties, such as GitHub, LinkedIn, Matrix, ETSI, and the Federal
          Ministry of Research, Technology and Space (BMFTR). Apart from our own
          platform presences described above, this privacy policy applies only
          to this website. When you follow such a link, the privacy policy of
          the respective operator applies; we have no influence on their data
          processing. No data is transmitted to these third parties merely by
          visiting our website; a connection is only established when you
          actively click a link.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Your rights</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Under the GDPR, you have the following rights with respect to personal
          data concerning you:
        </p>
        <ul
          class="list-disc pl-6 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-1"
        >
          <li>the right of access (Art. 15 GDPR),</li>
          <li>the right to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR),</li>
          <li>the right to erasure (Art. 17 GDPR),</li>
          <li>the right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR),</li>
          <li>the right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR).</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
          <strong class="text-foreground">
            Under Art. 21 GDPR, you have the right to object, on grounds
            relating to your particular situation, at any time to the processing
            of personal data concerning you which is based on Art. 6(1)(e) or
            (f) GDPR. This applies in particular to the processing based on our
            legitimate interests described in this privacy policy.
          </strong>
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
          To exercise these rights, please contact the controller using the
          contact details given above.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection
          supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR). The supervisory authority
          responsible for us is:
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Der Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz Niedersachsen<br />
          Prinzenstraße 5<br />
          30159 Hannover<br />
          Germany
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Website:{" "}
          <a
            href="https://www.lfd.niedersachsen.de"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          >
            www.lfd.niedersachsen.de
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          No automated decision-making
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          We do not use automated decision-making or profiling within the
          meaning of Art. 22 GDPR.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          We will update this privacy policy whenever the way this website
          processes data changes, e.g., if forms, embedded content, or analytics
          are added in the future.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Last updated: August 9, 2026
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
